                <pb facs="0545" n="425" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg425"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">813.00 Tacoma/–: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-23T10:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 23,
                                1922—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 3 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>44. Message to President Acosta from three Presidents participating in conference
                    aboard United States Ship <hi rendition="#italic">Tacoma</hi> states they have
                    signed agreement in which is clause asking Costa Rica to adhere. Uncertainty as
                    to contents of agreement and fact that conference was held and agreement reached
                    to which Costa Rica is asked to subscribe without having been previously
                    informed seriously complicates the situation here. Lack of information seriously
                    handicaps and embarrasses this Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
